aRepository.update` → `MangaRepositoryImpl.partialUpdate` → SQL `update` (governed chain). Read/filter: `mangas.updates_snoozed_until` → `updatesView`'s own `WHERE` clause (baked in, not a per-query parameter) → all 3 existing Updates queries automatically exclude snoozed rows → `UpdatesViewModel` (no changes needed to its filter-combination logic — snoozed rows never reach it, so `applyFilters`/`hasActiveFilters`/category filters compose exactly as today over the remaining rows).\n\n### Change Strategy\n1. Domain model: add `updatesSnoozedUntil` to `Manga`/`MangaUpdate` (governed).\n2. Data layer: thread the field through `MangaMapper`/`MangaRepositoryImpl` (governed).\n3. Schema: add column + migration `15.sqm` (ungoverned, adjacent to governed data cell).\n4. Feed query: one-line addition to `updatesView`'s base `WHERE` (ungoverned) — chosen over per-query `:now` parameters because it's DRY (one place, not three), requires zero Kotlin signature changes, and naturally composes with every existing/future consumer of the view.\n5. New interactor `SetMangaUpdatesSnooze` (ungoverned, but same package/pattern as governed `domain/manga` cell's sibling interactors).\n6. UI: manga-details overflow action + updates-list bulk action, both opening a shared snooze-picker dialog; UI reads current snooze state directly off `Manga.updatesSnoozedUntil` (already flows through existing `GetManga`/state).\n7. i18n strings.\n\n### Specification Impact\n`domain/manga/model` CODEMANIFEST: `Manga` and `MangaUpdate` signatures gain `updatesSnoozedUntil` — property/annotation additions only, reconciled in Step 7.\n`data/manga` CODEMANIFEST: `MangaMapper.mapManga` annotation's \"not individually listed here for brevity\" column list implicitly covers it (no signature shown in manifest for that method beyond the abbreviated form) — annotation text may get one clarifying line, reconciled in Step 7.\n`domain/manga/repository` CODEMANIFEST: no change (verified `update`/`updateAll` annotations already cover arbitrary `MangaUpdate` fields).\n\n### Usage Impact\n`sqldelight_row_mapper` (data/manga `.usages`... actually inline in CODEMANIFEST `Usages`, not a `.usages/*.md` file): description remains accurate as-is (\"mapper lambda receives the row's columns as individual typed parameters\") — no rewrite needed, only verified compatible.\n\n### Compatibility Verification\n**Backward compatible.** All three governed-cell changes are additive with default/optional values; no existing call site (all confirmed named-argument, no positional construction found repo-wide) breaks; no existing method signature removed or altered; no existing test exists for these types (confirmed via repo-wide search). Confirmed in Investigation Report's Breaking Change Assessment — all six questions answered NO.\n\n### Test Strategy\n- Unit test for `SetMangaUpdatesSnooze` interactor (mirrors `UpdateMangaNotes` pattern) — verifies it builds the correct `MangaUpdate` and delegates to the repository.\n- No existing test suite covers `MangaMapper`/`MangaRepositoryImpl`/SqlDelight queries directly (confirmed absent) — consistent with existing coverage baseline, not introducing a gap relative to sibling fields (`notes`, `favorite`, etc. are equally untested at this layer).\n- Manual/verify-skill pass on the SQL filtering logic (`updatesView` WHERE clause) since SQLDelight `.sq` files aren't unit-testable in isolation here without a test DB harness that doesn't currently exist for this module.\n\n### Risk Assessment\n| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| SQLite `strftime('%s','now')` timezone/precision mismatch with Kotlin-stored millis | Low | Low | `strftime('%s','now')` is UTC epoch seconds, consistent with Kotlin `Clock.System.now().toEpochMilliseconds()`; ×1000 conversion is exact; snooze granularity is day/week so second-level precision is irrelevant |\n| Forgetting to update all 3 `mapManga`-family functions in `MangaMapper` consistently | Medium | Medium